                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[i] Socketeer [/i] is a roguelite where you can hack into enemies to gain their special abilities. I initially gave this game a negative review due to frustrating UI problems, but I decided to change the rating because the patches have fixed most of the issues - such as playing tutorial over and over. The last few updates made the pacing of the game a little bit more enjoyable, which is very important for a game with one life. As with most roguelites, you have a procedural level generation, random shops with upgrades, and a few twists that are unique to this title. The \"decompression\" is a big mechanic in this game, anytime you blow up the wall you might get sucked into space, creating some funny and unexpected deaths. \n\nAnother thing that I really like about this title, is a freedom that you get when it comes to how you want to complete the level. Sure you could go and look for a key to the door, but you can also just put a bomb next to it (breaking some gaming logic right there). If you come across a teleport item, then you can just complete the level in a few seconds, although you will need to stop for energy eventually. You can even take the risk of killing a shop owner and not paying for any of the items; or just hack into him in to use one of the most powerful weapons in the game. Overall I don't have any complaints in regards to gameplay because it's pretty dynamic, even though the upgrade system is very basic (only a few items). \n\n[h1] Pros: [/h1]\n\n+ fun concept / interesting mechanics \n+ hacking into many playable robots\n+ you can change controls\n+ awesome soundtrack\n+ very good use of achievements\n\n[h1] Con: [/h1]\n\n- very basic upgrade system \n- seldom, but frustrating glitches\n\n[b] Overall Thoughts: 7/10 [/b]\n\nThe developer took my feedback and made the hacking controls more intuitive, making the game significantly more enjoyable. It does not have complex RPG elements so it probably won't keep you playing for too long, but its unorthodox mechanics make it very fun for a couple of hours.\n\n[code]Review By: http://store.steampowered.com/curator/31294838-Hidden-Gem-Discovery/ [/code]",
